WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 3 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:04.336
You own support knowledge for the fictional Harbor team.

00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:10.016
A new colleague must diagnose a delayed demo export without guessing whom to contact.

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:13.093
Existing notes say: ‘Exports slow sometimes.

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:14.165
Refresh.

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:21.616
Ask Morgan.’ Your deliverable is a runbook that a new support analyst can follow using the synthetic training environment.

00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:27.661
Before creating content, search the intended knowledge space for an existing export runbook.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:29.479
Compare scope and currency.

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:36.055
Update a suitable canonical page through the team’s process rather than leaving two competing instructions.

00:00:36.295 --> 00:00:41.799
If none exists, identify a parent location where analysts already look for procedures.

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:48.057
Choose a Confluence page for this exercise because the team wants a deliberate publishing checkpoint.

00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:56.489
Confluence also provides live docs, where changes appear as collaboration happens; do not treat those as unpublished page drafts.

00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:01.209
Current interface and content options may differ by rollout and subscription.

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:13.260
Worked plan: reader = new support analyst; task = decide whether a demo export is still processing or requires escalation; location = Harbor Support /

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:21.953
Runbooks; title = ‘Check a delayed demo export’; owner = Support Knowledge Owner; review trigger = workflow change.

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:24.497
These names and locations are fictional.

00:01:25.187 --> 00:01:26.275
Now it's your turn.

00:01:26.515 --> 00:01:29.501
You find an existing current runbook with the same scope.

00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:30.723
What should you do?

00:01:30.963 --> 00:01:34.077
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

